                        <field name="dc_subject">Ferdinand VII, King of Spain, 1784-1833 </field>
                        <field name="dc_title">The King. Since the divine Providence by means of the spontaneous and solemn renunciation of my august Father put me on the throne of my elders... and from that Faust day I entered the capital, in the midst of the most sincere demonstrations of love and loyalty with which the people of Madrid came out to receive me... I put in my Real spirit... dedicate all my time... to repair the evils that could give occasion the pernicious influence of a valid during the previous reynado... [Printed text] </field>
